2852:/// Wraps a [_BlockRenderer] so that the underlying block widget (and its
2853:/// [_TextSelectionSurface] children, geometry registration, and text-layout
2854:/// cache) stay mounted even when scrolled out of the viewport — but only when
2855:/// [keepAlive] is true. Used to keep the caret block and selection endpoints
2856:/// alive under editor virtualisation, so the caret and selection
2857:/// highlight always paint and the geometry registry always knows their box.
2858:///
2859:/// Also drives incremental rebuild: a block is only re-rendered when its
2860:/// content changed ([blockChanged]) *or* when the selection / caret / IME
2861:/// composition touches it. A pure caret move inside a different block leaves
2862:/// this block's cached child intact, avoiding the inline-span rebuild that
2863:/// would otherwise run for every block on every keystroke.
